      "created_at": "2024-03-24T18:40:04Z",
      "updated_at": "2024-03-24T19:22:10Z",
      "body": "[Test_Mac_M2.mov.zip](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/files/14736414/Test_Mac_M2.mov.zip)\r\nI have now also tested it on my **Mac mini M2 and it works perfectly**.\r\nBut I was able to determine at what moment Windows crashes compared to the Mac version. If I display the \"SDF Iters\" on the Mac version, the components become invisible at the point where Windows would crash. When I move the component back, the components appear again. \r\nMaybe this will help you to fix the error in the Windows version or is at least a clue :)\r\n(see also video in the attachment)\r\n\r\nI will now also test it on Linux and give feedback.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nUPDATE:\r\nIt also **works on Linux** and looks exactly like the video I recorded on the Mac Mini M2 :)\r\n\r\nI have seen that whenever the geometries disappear as shown in the video, this warning appears in the terminal:\r\n\r\nWARNING: The pre-allocated visual geometry buffer is full. Increase maxgeom above 20000. time = 2.6790.\r\n\r\nWARNING: The pre-allocated visual geometry buffer is full. Increase maxgeom above 20000. time = 2.0610.\r\n\r\nWARNING: Pre-assigned visual geometry buffer is full. Increase maxgeom above 20000. time = 0.4750.\r\n\r\n**So it seems to be a Windows Only bug.**",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
